  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "parseNextLayer",
    "file": "PcapPlusPlus/Packet++/src/NflogLayer.cpp",
    "description": "NflogLayer::parseNextLayer() trusts the NFULA_PAYLOAD TLV's record length and computes `payloadLen = payloadInfo.getTotalSize() - 4` without verifying that the total size is at least the 4-byte NFLOG TLV header. NflogTlv::canAssign() permits undersized records (it only requires enough bytes for the 2-byte length field), so a payload TLV with recordLen 1-3 is accepted and the unsigned subtraction underflows to a huge size. That bogus length is propagated to IPv6Layer; the eventual heap-buffer-overflow occurs in IPv6Layer::parseExtensions()/IPv6Extension::getExtensionLen() when extension fields are read beyond the actual packet buffer.",
    "conditions": "A captured packet must be decoded as NFLOG, have address family 10 (IPv6), and contain a malformed TLV recognized as NFULA_PAYLOAD (type 9) whose declared total size is smaller than the 4-byte TLV header; this PoV uses a 3-byte record. parseNextLayer() sets the payload pointer to recordValue, underflows `3 - 4` to SIZE_MAX, and IPv6Layer::isDataValid() therefore accepts the nominal length. Bytes following the malformed TLV must make the IPv6 next-header field identify a supported IPv6 extension, causing parseExtensions() to dereference extension header bytes outside the real RawPacket allocation."
  },
